    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0351" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Hungary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Brentano</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-23T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23,
                                1924—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 24—12:07
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Your December 22, 3 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d171-f1"/> and January 18, 7
                    p.m.” Foreign Office writes that the Government authorizes the aviators to fly
                    over and land in Hungary and that it will inform me later regarding landing
                    points and restrictions against photography.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Brentano</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
